# Copy to `docker/.env` (beside this file) — `cp docker/.env.example docker/.env`.
#
# ONE file serves both run modes, which is why it lives here rather than at the repo root: Compose reads
# `.env` from its project directory, which is the folder holding compose.yaml, and `./dev.sh` reads this
# same path for the native run (it must — Bun does not walk up for a `.env`, and the worker has no dotenv
# dependency at all). Point ENCORE_ENV_FILE elsewhere to override.
#
# RELATIVE PATHS IN HERE RESOLVE AGAINST docker/, NOT THE REPO ROOT, for anything Compose interpolates —
# that is ENCORE_DATA_VOLUME and ENCORE_MEDIA_VOLUME below. Use absolute paths for those two and the
# question does not arise. (DATA_DIR/MEDIA_DIR are different: compose.yaml sets them to in-container paths
# and dev.sh overrides them to absolute host paths, announcing it, so the values here are inert.)

# Encore core
PORT=3000
HOST=0.0.0.0

# SQLite (WAL) location. Created on first boot; no separate migrate step.
DATA_DIR=./data
# ENCORE_EPHEMERAL=1   # in-memory DB instead — a throwaway instance that persists nothing

# MediaStore backend: `local` (default, one box) or `object` (MinIO/S3 for remote workers)
MEDIA_STORE=local
MEDIA_DIR=./media

# Storage classes, split by REPLACEABILITY (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §2). Each defaults under MEDIA_DIR.
# ENCORE_AUDIO_DIR=./media/audio       # raw originals — NOT regenerable; this is what to back up
# ENCORE_DERIVED_DIR=./media/derived   # stems/pitch/lyrics/thumbs — safe to delete, recomputable
# ENCORE_META_DIR=./media/meta         # sidecar records — the authoritative library

# ── DOCKER ONLY: which HOST directories the containers mount ─────────────────────────────────────
# A property of the host's disks, so it belongs here rather than in a compose override. Both default to
# `../data` and `../media` — relative to docker/, i.e. the repo root. Set them ABSOLUTE: a relative value
# here resolves against docker/ too, which is rarely what anyone means.
#
# Core and the worker BOTH mount ENCORE_MEDIA_VOLUME and must agree, or core serves a path the worker
# never wrote to. On WSL2 these MUST point at the distro's own ext4 and never at /mnt/c — 9p does not
# honour POSIX locking and core runs SQLite in WAL mode (docs/deploy/WSL2.md).
# ENCORE_DATA_VOLUME=/srv/encore/data
# ENCORE_MEDIA_VOLUME=/srv/encore/media
# ENCORE_MEDIA_MAX_GB=20               # soft cap; evicts derived/ LRU-first. Unset = never delete

# TV "Next up" reveal ms (0 = gapless hard-cut). Seeded on FIRST BOOT only; Settings → Room owns it after.
# ENCORE_SONG_INTRO_MS=2500
# INTERSTITIAL_MS=2500   # DEPRECATED alias for ENCORE_SONG_INTRO_MS — still read, prefer the name above

# Address the TV's join QR advertises. Unset = derive from the request; set it where /tv's host cannot
# reach its own public address (WSL2, or a proxy forwarding no X-Forwarded-* headers). "Global → Joining"
# overrides it per runtime with no restart.
# ENCORE_PUBLIC_ORIGIN=http://10.69.1.169:3000

# Object-store (only when MEDIA_STORE=object) — docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §2. S3_BUCKET is required; without it
# Encore falls back to the local store rather than failing to boot. Credentials come from the standard
# AWS_* vars that Bun.S3Client reads directly — there is no S3_ACCESS_KEY setting.
# S3_ENDPOINT=http://minio:9000
# S3_BUCKET=encore-media
# S3_REGION=us-east-1
# S3_PREFIX=encore/
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# Worker (`./dev.sh compose --profile stems up`). Without one, make-karaoke requests sit at `queued` forever.
ENCORE_CORE_WS=ws://core:3000/ws?role=worker
ENCORE_WORKER_CONCURRENCY=1
# LEAVE THIS UNSET. The worker PROVES what it can do at startup by probing PATH and imports, and this
# setting can only NARROW that — so naming a subset here silently refuses the jobs the box could have run.
# Valid tokens, if you ever do need to narrow: fetch:ytdlp, stems, stems:roformer, stems:audiosep,
# stems:ensemble, align, diarize. Anything else is dropped as unprovable with a warning.
# ENCORE_WORKER_CAPABILITIES=
# Shared secret on role=worker WS upgrades; SAME value both sides. UNSET on core = worker registration is
# UNAUTHENTICATED, so anything that can reach the port can register and receive jobs.
# ENCORE_WORKER_TOKEN=
# ENCORE_WORKER_ID=worker-1
# ENCORE_DEMUCS_MODEL=htdemucs
# Forces the accelerator: cpu | cuda | xpu | mps. Unset means auto-detect, which is what you want; naming
# one makes an unreachable device CRASH at startup instead of cooking silently on the CPU, so set it only
# when you want a passthrough or driver mistake to be loud. Metal is unreachable from a container — a Mac
# worker has to be a native run (docs/deploy/README.md).
# ENCORE_DEVICE=
# ENCORE_WHISPERX_DEVICE=cpu          # `cuda` on a GPU box
# The next two are FALLBACKS only: core sends asrModel/syncMode per `align` job and that value wins.
# ENCORE_ASR_MODEL=base               # Whisper checkpoint used to transcribe the vocals stem
# ENCORE_SYNC_MODE=forced             # timing fidelity: `forced` (per-word) or line-level
# ENCORE_PROCESSOR=stub               # no-ML placeholder artifacts — tests plumbing, does NOT play
